## Gfx::PaintingSurface::Impl (Libraries/LibGfx/PaintingSurface.cpp:28). Filled in by region r10:
## Skia is replaced (DESIGN.md §7.3), so the sk_sp<SkSurface> is the raster module drawing
## into the surface's bitmap (the donor's CPU path, where the SkSurface wraps the bitmap's
## pixels). `raster_pixels` is the premultiplied RGBA the raster module draws into between
## painting_surface_begin_raster and painting_surface_end_raster: the bitmap's own pixels when
## they already have that form, otherwise a buffer converted from and back to the bitmap.
pub struct PaintingSurfaceImpl:
    pub var context: SkiaBackendContext*?  # RefPtr<SkiaBackendContext>: always none (no GPU)
    pub var size: IntSize
    pub var bitmap: Bitmap*  # RefPtr<Bitmap>: never null on the CPU path
    pub var raster_pixels: u8[]
    pub var raster_aliases_bitmap: bool
    pub var raster_depth: u32  # begin_raster nesting

## SkCanvas (Libraries/LibGfx/PaintingSurface.h:29): opaque in this phase (not in the phase-1 closure).
pub struct SkCanvas:
    pub var opaque_: u8

